From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:10:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Build with Soong

The Android image build compiles TalkBack from this tree with Soong, as
it does the other applications it ships. Each module's Android.bp lists
the sources of the Gradle module's phone variant (src/main and
src/phone), links the resources with transitive R classes as the Gradle
build leaves them, and takes the library versions the platform carries.

This part holds the license, the proguard annotations, the utils module
with the BuildConfig the Gradle build would generate for a release
build, the braille modules, the material preference modules, the
service and settings module with its BuildConfig and app_id string, and
the app with the manifest that names its package and application class.
The two provider authorities of the service's manifest, which the Gradle
build fills in from the application ID, are written out. The translation
and key tables the Gradle build zips into res/raw become genrules, and
liblouis and BRLTTY with its braille drivers build as native libraries
against the NDK API level of the app's minSdk, with the platform's JNI
headers. The ndk-build makefiles of the braille libraries carry a
.find-ignore, so that the platform makefile search leaves them alone.

The libraries take the app's minimum SDK (26), so that the manifest
merge accepts them in an app of that minimum.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
